@startuml
' A loop that starts with an action (`repeat :text;`): the way back leads
' to it, as to the mark a plain `repeat` starts with; a note after its
' `backward` stands beside the action on the way back.
start
repeat :Enter data;
  :Submit;
  backward :Warning;
  note right: Shown in red
repeat while (Valid?) is (No) not (Yes)
->saved;
repeat :Read a line;
  :Parse it;
repeat while (More lines?) is (yes)
stop
@enduml
